{{also|tüb}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|tubbe}}, {{m|enm|tobbe}}, from {{der|en|dum|tubbe}} or {{der|en|gml|tubbe}}, {{m|gml|tobbe}}, further etymology unknown. Considered to be unrelated to {{m|en|tube}}.<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|tŭb}}, {{IPA|en|/tʌb/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-tub.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌb|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
[[File:Tub of cottage cheese.jpg|thumb|Tub of cottage cheese, lid, and lidding film]]

# A [[flat]]-[[bottomed]] [[vessel]], of [[width]] similar to or greater than its [[height]], used for [[storing]] or [[packing]] things, or for [[washing]] things in.
#: {{ux|en|He bought a '''tub''' of lard to roast the potatoes in.}}
# The [[content]]s or [[capacity]] of such a vessel.
#: {{ux|en|She added a '''tub''' of margarine to the stew.}}
# A [[bathtub]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1920|author=Theodore Sharpe|title=My Place in the Shade: And Various Verse|page=27
|passage=Teach me to love my morning '''tub''', / In waters cold to splash and rub; / O, grant my Turkish towel may flood / Its virtues through my soul and blood.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical|informal}} A [[slow]]-[[moving]] [[craft]].
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Drachinifel|title=The Russian 2nd Pacific Squadron - Voyage of the Damned|date=13 March 2019|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9Mdi_Fh9_Ag|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221015053242/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9Mdi_Fh9_Ag|archivedate=15 October 2022|accessdate=15 October 2022|time=24:52|text=But, with any ships in the Baltic Fleet that were worth sending - and some that probably ''weren't'' worth sending anyway - having ''already'' been dispatched, this gave him the perfect excuse to start rounding up old, obsolete vessels which had been rejected in the first place as being old '''tubs''' and designated by some of the less-kind officers as the "Sink-by-Themselves Squadron".}}
# {{lb|en|humorous|or|derogatory}} Any structure shaped like a tub, such as a certain old form of [[pulpit]], a short broad [[boat]], etc.
#* {{RQ:South Twelve Sermons|passage=All being took up and busied, some in pulpits and some in '''tubs''', in the grand work of preaching and holding forth.}}
# A small [[cask]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''tub''' of gin}}
# Any of various historically designated quantities of goods to be sold by the tub (butter, oysters, etc).
# {{lb|en|mining}} A box or bucket in which [[coal]] or [[ore]] is sent up a [[shaft]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[sweat]]ing in a tub; a [[tub fast]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Timon of Athens|4|3|passage='''tubs''' and baths; bring down rose-cheeked youth <br>To the tub-fast and the diet}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A corpulent or obese person.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|author=Trey Ellis|title=Platitudes: & the New Black Aesthetic|page=139
|passage=Donald tells him to be more realistic. Take those two girls over there, for example. One's a zitface and the other's a '''tub''', so they'd be perfect for them.}}

